## Issue delivery handoff

<The accepted-members table is the authoritative candidate list; related
nonmembers are not closure targets. Give each member explicit, individually
checkable criteria. Implementation must evaluate every criterion and retain
resolved/partial/unresolved outcomes. This plan grants no closure authority.>

The operator may approve ordinary local implementation or explicitly invoke
`$implement`. Only the latter produces the Implement evidence/receipt. Any
closure request must be separate direct-user intent; authorized PR
work adds closing references only after per-issue validation and a concise
verified comment. GitHub closes those issues on default-branch merge when
repository settings permit it. Partial or unverified issues remain open.

## Maintainer handoff

After triage, the root offers the exact ready plan/member set with its owning
project and waits for direct approval unless already authorized. Natural approval
uses ordinary local implementation; explicit `$implement` uses its existing
workflow. Refresh exact plan bytes and evidence before either route. Commit and
publication retain their owning authorization. This plan does not implement or publish the change,
schedule delivery, or certify completion.
